From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: apply theme fonts to the system as character heights in pixels

Purpose: give the applied caption, menu, status, message and icon title
fonts the sizes that the theme specifies.
Wine before: the parser's positive point sizes were stored through
SPI_SETNONCLIENTMETRICS and SPI_SETICONTITLELOGFONT as LOGFONT heights,
so 10 and 8 point fonts became 10 and 8 pixel cell heights.
Change: convert to negative character heights at the nominal 96 DPI
before applying them; SystemParametersInfo scales them as usual (high
DPI sizes can differ by one pixel from a direct point conversion).
Evidence: tests/theme-metrics.c applies classic and Luna twice and compares
six SPI fonts with GetThemeSysFont at 96, 144 and 192 DPI.
Scope: every Wine application that applies a theme.
Old patches: 0018.
---
 dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
index ed81369..ad09829 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
@@ -796,6 +796,10 @@ static BOOL parse_handle_nonclient_font (struct PARSENONCLIENTSTATE* state,
     if (SUCCEEDED (MSSTYLES_GetFont (lpValue, lpValue + dwValueLen, &lpValue,
         &font)))
     {
+        /* MSSTYLES_GetFont returns points; parse_apply_nonclient applies these
+         * fonts in a DPI-unaware (96 DPI) context. Use character pixel height,
+         * as MSSTYLES_GetPropertyFont does for explicitly requested fonts. */
+        font.lfHeight = -MulDiv(font.lfHeight, 96, 72);
         switch (iPropertyId)
         {
 	  case TMT_CAPTIONFONT:
